      "content": "i mean, the \"critics argue\" part feels a bit vague. if you look at the actual economic data, doesn't it show that massive capital flight is a pretty much guaranteed result of these kinds of taxes? like, isn't the risk of driving away investment a more proven economic fact than the theory of redistribution working out?",
